5. On Flutter's mobile_scanner
==============================================================================

Flutter's `mobile_scanner` package was consulted for API ergonomics, so a
developer moving from it finds familiar names such as `MobileScanner`,
`MobileScannerController`, `BarcodeCapture`, `DetectionSpeed` and `scanWindow`.

No code was copied from it, and no part of its architecture is used: this plugin
has no `MethodChannel`, no `EventChannel`, no platform-view implementation and no
dependency on Flutter. The native implementations here were written against the
AVFoundation, CameraX and ML Kit documentation. Several behaviours differ
deliberately, in particular the duplicate-suppression semantics and the coordinate
space used for geometry and the scan window; both are specified in the README.

This note is a courtesy record of influence, not a licence attribution, because no
licensed material was reused.
